# s4_param_release (off-path)
#
# basis      s3_beaver_reveal_inplace peak 2693096 kB; second attempt on its largest object (first:
#            off-path/s4_param_stream/, 0.74% vs 0.812% spread). Single pool (host).
# object     heap:libc10.so+0x4a675, 1916.0 MB (69.5%); dominant occupant the encrypted parameter set:
#            201 Parameter modules, 866494480 B int64 shares; Constant 3564 B; else zero
#            (steps/s3_beaver_reveal_inplace/evidence/graphowners_party0.txt).
# reducible  Module.encrypt() creates all 201 shares before the first operation; peak at the first
#            operation reads one (reloadable condition).
# missed     anon:[heap] 383.6 -> 555.3 MB in the first attempt: 2.36 MB shares served from the arena,
#            free returns them to glibc.
# fix        1. MALLOC_MMAP_THRESHOLD_=131072 in the environment (mmap-served, munmap on free; disables the
#               dynamic threshold that grows to 32 MiB; must precede interpreter start).
#            2. malloc_trim(0) after the spill; return value and recovered RSS logged.
# draws      encryption order and sizes unchanged before spill; same int64 bytes back. Rewrap avoids
#            MPCTensor.shallow_copy() (MPCTensor([]) would take a PRZS on an empty size).
# spill      node-local rootfs (/proc/mounts, logged), tmpfs refused, not mmap'd (file: excluded from W).
#            866 MiB: write 0.36 s, read 0.14 s.
# enabler    none.
#
# pool_attacked: host
# object_attacked: libc10.so+0x4a675
OMP_NUM_THREADS=8
MALLOC_MMAP_THRESHOLD_=131072
SHAFT_LEVERS=plaintext_free_cpu,triple_share_free_cpu,beaver_reveal_inplace_cpu,param_release_cpu
